chapter.v:
	May the 

	 stars of its morning be dark;May it look for light, but have none,And not see the dawning of the day;
 [Num. 11:15; 1 Kin. 19:4; Job]

	Or with 

	 princes who had gold,Who filled their houses with silver;
 [Ps. 38:11 j Jer.]

	Who long 

	 for death, but it does not come,And search for it more than hidden treasures;
 [Job 13:4 o Ps.]
